.TH SYSINFOVIEWER 1 "November 2024" "sysinfoviewer 0.2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysinfoviewer \- comprehensive system information viewer with real-time monitoring
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysinfoviewer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysinfoviewer
is a comprehensive graphical system information viewer built with wxWidgets for Linux systems. It provides real-time monitoring and detailed information about your system's hardware, software, and resource usage.
.PP
The application displays system information across four main categories:
.PP
.B System Information
- Real-time CPU, memory, and disk usage with visual doughnut charts
.br
- Battery information including health, charge cycles, and time estimates
.br
- Operating system details and user information
.PP
.B Processes/Threads
- Live process monitoring sorted by CPU usage
.br
- Detailed information including PID, user, CPU%, RAM%, and command
.br
- Process management capabilities
.PP
.B Miscellaneous Information
- Network interface details with upload/download speeds
.br
- Display information including resolution, refresh rate, and EDID data
.br
- Storage device enumeration with usage statistics
.br
- Audio device detection and capabilities
.br
- Motherboard and BIOS information
.br
- Detailed CPU information with per-core usage monitoring
.PP
.B Installed Applications
- Complete list of installed packages (Arch Linux)
.br
- Package details including version, size, dependencies, and installation date

.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Real-time Monitoring
CPU usage updated every second with visual feedback
.br
Memory and disk usage with color-coded indicators
.br
Network speed monitoring with total data transfer statistics
.br
Per-core CPU usage gauges
.TP
.B Battery Management
Comprehensive battery information for laptops
.br
Battery health percentage calculation
.br
Charge cycle counting
.br
Time to full/empty estimation
.br
Power consumption monitoring
.TP
.B Hardware Detection
Automatic detection of audio devices via ALSA
.br
Display information via xrandr and DRM
.br
Storage device enumeration from /proc/mounts
.br
Network interface detection
.br
Motherboard information from DMI tables
.TP
.B Process Management
Process listing with detailed information
.br
Sorting by CPU usage
.br
Total process count display
.br
Process name extraction from command line

.SH OPTIONS
.B sysinfoviewer
does not currently accept command-line options. All configuration is done through the graphical interface.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B sysinfoviewer
requires the following system components:
.TP
.B wxWidgets 3.2.5+
GUI framework (wxwidgets-gtk3)
.TP
.B curl
For potential network operations
.TP
.B ALSA
Audio device detection (alsa-lib)
.TP
.B DRM/KMS
Display information via Direct Rendering Manager
.TP
.B /proc filesystem
System information retrieval
.TP
.B /sys filesystem
Hardware information from sysfs

.SH OPTIONAL DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B lm_sensors
Enhanced hardware monitoring support
.TP
.B smartmontools
Disk health information via S.M.A.R.T.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B /proc/cpuinfo
CPU information and specifications
.TP
.B /proc/stat
CPU usage statistics
.TP
.B /proc/meminfo
Memory usage information
.TP
.B /proc/mounts
Mounted filesystem information
.TP
.B /proc/net/dev
Network interface statistics
.TP
.B /proc/net/route
Network routing information
.TP
.B /sys/class/power_supply/
Battery information
.TP
.B /sys/class/backlight/
Display brightness information
.TP
.B /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/
Motherboard and BIOS information
.TP
.B /dev/dri/
Direct Rendering Manager devices for display info

.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Show system information summary dialog
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit application (standard exit)

.SH EXAMPLES
To launch the system information viewer:
.PP
.nf
.RS
$ sysinfoviewer
.RE
.fi
.PP
The application will open with a tabbed interface showing:
.br
1. System Information (default view)
.br
2. Processes/Threads
.br
3. Miscellaneous Info
.br
4. Installed Applications

.SH NOTES
.TP
.B Permissions
Some information may require elevated permissions to access. The application will gracefully handle permission denied errors.
.TP
.B Platform Support
This application is designed specifically for Linux systems and uses Linux-specific APIs and file systems.
.TP
.B Battery Detection
Battery information is only available on systems with battery hardware (laptops, tablets). Desktop systems will show "No battery found."
.TP
.B Package Management
Application listing currently supports Arch Linux and derivatives using pacman. Other distributions may not display installed applications.

.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B No battery information
Ensure /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0 exists and is readable
.TP
.B Missing display information
Install xrandr and ensure X11 or Wayland with XWayland is running
.TP
.B No audio devices detected
Verify ALSA is properly configured: aplay -l
.TP
.B Process list empty
Check permissions for /proc filesystem access

.SH BUGS
Known issues:
.br
- Application listing is Arch Linux specific (pacman)
.br
- Some EDID parsing may fail on certain displays
.br
- Network statistics reset on interface changes
.PP
Report bugs to: https://github.com/Magpiny/sysinfoviewer/issues

